I don't see a call to lavaan in your R syntax, so I'm still not sure how you identify your constructs (e.g., std.lv <http://std.lv> = TRUE?).  But I would think you might have trouble identifying a second-order construct with only 2 first-order constructs.  You don't gain any information by doing this, and it might be necessary to identify Loy either by fixing the latent variance of Loy to 1, and constraining its loadings on Com and Rec to equality.  Or to identify Loy by fixing by loadings to 1 and freely estimating its variance, which would be identical to the estimated (residual) covariance between Com and Rec if you were to exclude Loy from the model.

Terry

